 "evidence": {
  "formulas": "Acyl group + S + R, the convention of acetyl-ACP C2H3OSR, malonyl-ACP C3H3O3SR, octanoyl-ACP C8H15OSR and ACP1 HSR. Replaces placeholders 'ACP' (read as elements A, C, P), 'C141'/'C161' (read as 141/161 carbons), formulas with '*', or none.",
  "protons": "The block copies BiGG iMM904/iND750 stoichiometry written for ionized species; with the model's neutral acyl and fatty-acid species one H+ is surplus in each condensation, hydrolysis and elongation lump. The remaining -1 charge per NADPH is the model-wide NADP(+) (m178) convention.",
  "hydrolase_direction": "Thioester hydrolysis is strongly exergonic: eQuilibrator estimates dG'0 = -29.6 +/- 12.6 kJ/mol (K'eq 1.6e5) and dG'm = -46.8 kJ/mol for palmitoyl-CoA + H2O = palmitate + CoA (pH 7.5, I 0.25 M), the analogous phosphopantetheine thioester. The reverse direction would make an acyl thioester from a free fatty acid without ATP. Making the 7 reversible cytosolic hydrolases forward-only (as R2217, R2220, R2223 already are) removes the C14->C16 cycle observed through R2226(reverse)/R2225/R2230/R2231/R2232.",
  "sources": [
   "https://equilibrator.weizmann.ac.il/search?query=palmitoyl-CoA+%2B+H2O+%3D+palmitate+%2B+CoA",
   "https://bigg.ucsd.edu/models/iMM904/reactions/FA180ACPH"
  ]
 }
